    <DataNode elementId="AT1G31800-MONOMER" textLabel="carotene beta-ring hydroxylase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q56YV8" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">A number of &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; mutants affected in the &lt;i&gt;LUT5&lt;/i&gt; gene were shown to be defective in the production of lutein (18% reduction) and accumulates two lutein biosynthesis-intermediate compounds: |FRAME:CPD1F-118| and |FRAME:CPD-7421|. Moreover, a reduction in total amounts of &amp;beta;,&amp;beta;-carotenoids is observed alongside an increase in total &amp;beta;,&amp;epsilon;-carotenoids |CITS:[16492736]|. It is therefore thought that the protein encoded by this gene possesses &amp;beta;-ring hydroxylase activity |CITS:[16492736]|. The enzyme has not been purified and characterized.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G31800-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G31800.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_564384" />
